From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:19:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: don't flush a legacy CTL after its interface has
 stopped

On DPU < 5.0 the CTL latches a flush at the next vsync of the interface
it drives.  dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup() runs after the video
encoder has switched the timing engine off, and still flushes the mixers
it has just reset, so the flush is never taken: the bits stay pending in
CTL_FLUSH, where a CTL soft reset doesn't clear them either.

The next display on that CTL then waits for a flush which can't
complete.  On SDA660, going back to fbcon from a two-mixer mode leaves
the LM_1 bit pending, and every following frame of the single-mixer
mode times out:

  [dpu error]vblank timeout: 80
  [dpu error]wait for commit done returned -110

Only trigger the flush from the teardown on DPU >= 5.0.  The legacy CTL
gets its registers flushed by its next user, as downstream does, which
rewrites CTL_TOP without a flush when it stops a CTL.

Fixes: 22cb02bc96ff ("drm/msm/disp/dpu: reset the datapath after timing engine disable")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>

[ from patchwork.kernel.org series 1178674, patch 1; not applied upstream yet ]
[ up3: rebased onto our queue's CTL_START change in dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup() (the DPU 13.x writeback-only CTL_START stays inside the new core_major_ver >= 5 branch; on kaanapali the behaviour is unchanged). ]
[ upstream author: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>; picked for the iceland kernel q89 ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 23 ++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
index d2d754e3f571..8df7f41811a3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -2341,16 +2341,19 @@ void dpu_encoder_helper_phys_cleanup(struct dpu_encoder_phys *phys_enc)
 	if (ctl->ops.reset_intf_cfg)
 		ctl->ops.reset_intf_cfg(ctl, &intf_cfg);
 
-	ctl->ops.trigger_flush(ctl);
-	/*
-	 * CTL_START kicks writeback here (command mode does not come here).
-	 * The video encoder never uses it: the timing engine latches the
-	 * flush. On DPU 13.x a CTL_START written once the timing engine is
-	 * off keeps the flush of an enable in the same commit (a modeset)
-	 * from latching, and the panel stays black.
-	 */
-	if (phys_enc->hw_wb)
-		ctl->ops.trigger_start(ctl);
+	/* a legacy CTL latches its flush at the vsync of a stopped interface */
+	if (phys_enc->dpu_kms->catalog->mdss_ver->core_major_ver >= 5) {
+		ctl->ops.trigger_flush(ctl);
+		/*
+		 * CTL_START kicks writeback here (command mode does not come
+		 * here). The video encoder never uses it: the timing engine
+		 * latches the flush. On DPU 13.x a CTL_START written once the
+		 * timing engine is off keeps the flush of an enable in the same
+		 * commit (a modeset) from latching, and the panel stays black.
+		 */
+		if (phys_enc->hw_wb)
+			ctl->ops.trigger_start(ctl);
+	}
 	ctl->ops.clear_pending_flush(ctl);
 }
 
